---
import Layout from '~/layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import { SITE } from 'astrowind:config';

const crumbs = [
  { name: 'Home', href: '/' },
  { name: 'R&D Center', href: '/randdcenter' },
  { name: 'Prototype Workshop' },
];

const metadata = {
  title: `Prototype Workshop — Full-Scale Pool Prototyping & Fill Testing | ${SITE.name}`,
  description: `From CAD to water-ready pool in 8-12 weeks. Our Prototype Workshop builds, outfits, and fill-tests custom drop-stitch inflatable pools. Start your prototype project today.`,
};
---

<Layout metadata={metadata} breadcrumbs={crumbs}>
  <section class="px-6 sm:px-6 py-16 sm:py-20 mx-auto max-w-5xl">
    <a href="/randdcenter" class="text-sm text-gray-500 hover:underline">&larr; Back to R&D Center</a>
    <div class="mt-4 grid md:grid-cols-5 gap-10">
      <div class="md:col-span-3">
        <p class="text-sm font-semibold text-primary uppercase tracking-wider">Lab 05</p>
        <h1 class="mt-2 text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold">Prototype Workshop</h1>
        <p class="mt-3 text-lg text-muted">From CAD model to water-ready pool — built, fitted, and proven</p>
      </div>
      <div class="md:col-span-2">
        <img
          src="https://assets.olagoon.com/images/olagoon/products/grand-lagoon.webp"
          alt="OLagoon prototype workshop pool fabrication"
          class="w-full h-48 object-cover rounded-xl"
        />
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="px-6 sm:px-6 pb-12 mx-auto max-w-4xl prose prose-gray dark:prose-invert">
    <h2>Where design becomes reality</h2>
    <p>
      A CAD model, no matter how detailed, cannot reveal how a pool will actually perform until it is pressurised and
      filled. That is why our Prototype Workshop is designed to translate engineering data into a physical, water-ready
      pool as quickly and accurately as possible. Every new {SITE.name} model — and every significant custom build — passes
      through this workshop before the production tooling is committed.
    </p>
    <p>
      The workshop is fully equipped for simultaneous fabrication of walls, chambers, and fittings. This
      parallel-workflow approach cuts prototype lead time to 8-12 weeks from engineering release, compared to the
      industry norm of 16-20 weeks. When your application demands a specialised solution, we can move from concept to a
      filled, validated pool in under three months.
    </p>

    <h2>Workshop capabilities</h2>
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th>Workstation</th><th>Equipment</th><th>Purpose</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr
          ><td>Wall &amp; floor fabrication</td><td
            >CNC fabric cutter, heat-lamination press, drop-stitch core preparation station</td
          ><td>Full-scale wall and floor production in all three construction types</td></tr
        >
        <tr
          ><td>Wall &amp; chamber assembly</td><td>RF welding press, hot-air tacking station, inflation test jig</td><td
            >Fabrication of full-size wall and chamber assemblies with all baffles and valves</td
          ></tr
        >
        <tr
          ><td>Fittings &amp; outfitting</td><td
            >Valve-mount jig, entry-step and handle welding fixtures, drain-fitting station</td
          ><td>Complete outfitting: valves, entry steps, drain fittings, handles, ground-sheet anchors</td></tr
        >
        <tr
          ><td>Instrumentation bay</td><td
            >Pressure transducers, strain gauges, water-level sensors, thermocouple array, data-logger</td
          ><td>Fill-test instrumentation installation and calibration</td></tr
        >
      </tbody>
    </table>

    <h2>The prototype journey — step by step</h2>
    <ol>
      <li>
        <strong>Engineering handover</strong> — The design package (3D model, FEA report, bill of materials, layup schedule)
        is formally reviewed by the workshop lead and the project engineer. Any manufacturing concerns are flagged and resolved
        before cutting begins.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Wall &amp; floor production</strong> — The drop-stitch core is built according to the engineering specification.
        For single-layer construction: the drop-stitch core is laminated with the specified PVC skin. For double-layer construction:
        the additional skin is applied over the base laminate before the pattern is cut. For fused construction: the lamination
        parameters are loaded from the approved process sheet and verified on a first-off coupon.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Wall fabrication</strong> — Fabric is cut using CNC-pattern templates, then RF-welded into full-size walls
        and chambers. Each chamber is inflated to test pressure and left for 24 h for initial stabilisation.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Assembly &amp; outfitting</strong> — Floor and walls are mated. Drain fittings and entry-step mounts are fitted,
        carry handles are installed, the inflation valve is torqued in, and the ground-sheet attachment points are aligned.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Static tests</strong> — Before the pool is filled, it undergoes: hydrostatic load verification (full water
        load + 30 % reserve), chamber pressure-hold test, valve leak-down test, handle and step pull-test.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Fill-and-load test programme</strong> –20 hours of hydrostatic and pressure testing, detailed below.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Prototype review</strong> — A formal sign-off meeting is held with engineering, production, and quality teams.
        Any required design changes are documented and incorporated into the production release.
      </li>
    </ol>

    <div class="not-prose my-10 p-6 rounded-xl bg-gray-50 dark:bg-gray-900 border border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-800">
      <p class="text-sm font-semibold text-gray-500 mb-3 uppercase tracking-wider">
        20-Hour Fill-and-Load Test Programme — Test Schedule
      </p>
      <div class="space-y-2 text-sm">
        <div class="flex items-center gap-3 p-2 rounded bg-white dark:bg-gray-950">
          <span class="w-12 text-xs font-bold text-blue-600">2 h</span><span class="flex-1"
            >Initial fill &amp; settlement — water level monitored to nominal line, chamber pressure baseline logged,
            visual seam inspection</span
          >
        </div>
        <div class="flex items-center gap-3 p-2 rounded bg-white dark:bg-gray-950">
          <span class="w-12 text-xs font-bold text-blue-600">4 h</span><span class="flex-1"
            >Pressure cycling — repeated inflate/deflate cycles across the 10–15 PSI operating band; strain gauges on
            wall seams</span
          >
        </div>
        <div class="flex items-center gap-3 p-2 rounded bg-white dark:bg-gray-950">
          <span class="w-12 text-xs font-bold text-blue-600">3 h</span><span class="flex-1"
            >Hydrostatic wall test — wall deflection measured at full water load; 20 cm rigid sit-on wall geometry
            verified</span
          >
        </div>
        <div class="flex items-center gap-3 p-2 rounded bg-white dark:bg-gray-950">
          <span class="w-12 text-xs font-bold text-blue-600">3 h</span><span class="flex-1"
            >Thermal exposure — wall surface temperature mapping under full sun; air-pressure drift logged against
            ambient heat</span
          >
        </div>
        <div class="flex items-center gap-3 p-2 rounded bg-white dark:bg-gray-950">
          <span class="w-12 text-xs font-bold text-blue-600">3 h</span><span class="flex-1"
            >Load case testing — simulated user loads on walls and floor; entry-step, handle, and ground-mat anchor pull
            tests</span
          >
        </div>
        <div class="flex items-center gap-3 p-2 rounded bg-white dark:bg-gray-950">
          <span class="w-12 text-xs font-bold text-blue-600">3 h</span><span class="flex-1"
            >Endurance soak — 3 h continuous full-water hold; monitoring of chamber pressure, seam condition, and water
            temperature</span
          >
        </div>
        <div class="flex items-center gap-3 p-2 rounded bg-white dark:bg-gray-950">
          <span class="w-12 text-xs font-bold text-blue-600">2 h</span><span class="flex-1"
            >Final inspection — controlled drain-down, post-test inspection of all components, tighten/check all
            fasteners, document findings</span
          >
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <h2>Custom prototyping for unique applications</h2>
    <p>
      The Prototype Workshop is where we solve the problems that standard production pools cannot address. Recent
      examples include:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        A quick-drain plunge-pool variant for a European hotel chain's rooftop terrace pilot across twelve properties,
        requiring a low-profile 20 cm wall, rapid drain-down between guest sessions, and a reinforced UV-stabilised
        outer skin — all prototyped, fitted, and tested at our facility.
      </li>
      <li>
        A cold-plunge variant for a Scandinavian wellness studio, with a 10–15 PSI pressure-cycled chamber specification
        rated for daily 4–6 &deg;C water operation and a thermal-cover anchoring system.
      </li>
      <li>
        A swim-lagoon line for a waterpark operator, where the prototype was used to validate wall rigidity, entry-step
        anchoring, and abrasion resistance against the concrete pad before the client committed to a six-lagoon
        installation.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Our prototyping team</h2>
    <p>
      The workshop is staffed by eight multi-skilled fabrication technicians, each cross-trained in at least two of the
      three core disciplines (wall, chamber, fitting). The team lead is a master fabricator with 16 years of experience
      spanning custom one-off builds to production series. Every prototype is assigned a dedicated project engineer who
      serves as the single point of contact for the client throughout the build and test process.
    </p>

    <h2>Client involvement</h2>
    <p>
      We actively encourage our clients to attend key milestones during the prototype build — particularly the initial
      fit-out review and the fill-and-load test. Your operational feedback during these stages is invaluable in
      fine-tuning the pool before it enters production. We do not build in a vacuum; we build in partnership with you.
    </p>
    <p>
      The 20-hour fill-and-load test is also an opportunity for your team to familiarise themselves with the pool's
      operation, fittings layout, and maintenance requirements, ensuring a smooth transition to service when the
      production pools are delivered.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="px-6 sm:px-6 pb-20 mx-auto max-w-4xl text-center">
    <div class="rounded-xl border border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-800 bg-gray-50 dark:bg-gray-900 p-8">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold">Start your prototype project</h2>
      <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-muted">
        Tell us about the pool you need and we will propose a prototype development plan.
      </p>
      <a
        href="/contact"
        class="mt-4 inline-block px-6 py-3 bg-primary text-white font-semibold rounded-md hover:bg-primary/90"
        >Contact our prototyping team</a
      >
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
